{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123647","id":4582192992,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABER63YA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123647","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123647.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123647.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123647","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123647/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123647/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123647/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/9102336eb0265e2ef5adb96c08ab411bca181daf","number":123647,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add Dual Quaternion Skinning to Mesh Instances","user":{"login":"iiMidknightii","id":89699177,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5Njk5MTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89699177?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii","html_url":"https://github.com/iiMidknightii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiMidknightii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"An implementation of https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9235.\r\nAlternative to the older implementation #89131.\r\n\r\n## For Reviewers:\r\nI didn't bother doing 2D mesh/skeleton skinning, but with some encouragement and pointers on what needs to be done, I think I could do it.\r\n\r\nI'm also not sure I handled the GLES3 shader correctly at all.  It's a bit more complicated than the Forward+ was.\r\n\r\n## Details:\r\n\r\nThis implementation is a variation of the source found (here)[https://users.cs.utah.edu/~ladislav/dq/index.html].  I properly attributed the original source in the shader code wherever I could.  \r\n\r\nThis doesn't actually change the CPU side bone transformation matrices either in mesh storage or the compute shader buffers.  Instead, this merely adds a new parameter uniform enumeration to decide which style of skinning is used.  The default path is to use traditional linear blend skinning.  I added 2 other methods, both variants of Dual Quaternion.  The first method is traditional dual quaternion skinning where all the scale/shear in the original bone transforms is lost.  There is technically an opportunity to reduce the bone transform storage and transfer sizes from 12 floats to 8, but I didn't modify that part of the pipeline.  The other version of dual quaternion skinning I added is a \"scaled\" dual quaternion which applies both dual quaternion skinning and the pure non-orthonormal part of the linear blend matrix to the final matrix.  \r\n\r\nRenderingServer now has a new enumeration MeshSkinningMethod with 3 values (for now).  That is set by the method \"instance_set_skinning_method\" for each mesh instance.  MeshInstance3D also duplicates the enumeration definition from RenderingServer with its own setters/getters.\r\n\r\n## Reference Test Project:\r\n[dual-quaternion-skinning.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32590699/dual-quaternion-skinning.zip)\r\n\r\nThis is a humanoid character that was made in Blender with \"preserve volume\" enabled to help keep certain... assets... from candy-striping while posing.  There are a few animations to test out the skinning.  Especially useful is the \"crouch\" animation since it deforms the lower torso and thigh areas quite a bit under LBS.  There is also some bone scaling thrown in to shakedown whether the scaling is applied correctly in conjunction with QDS.  See attached screenshots for some comparisons:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"3122\" height=\"1546\" alt=\"lbs_arms\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a54d705-ddcb-4c87-8764-d5d78e45ab9a\" />\r\n<img width=\"3120\" height=\"1545\" alt=\"dqs_arms\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/37231d04-07fc-432e-a971-8bc3c6d40ecc\" />\r\n<img width=\"3123\" height=\"1547\" alt=\"lbs_squat\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/61ae634f-ed86-430d-beaf-06fe1c9c73db\" />\r\n<img width=\"3125\" height=\"1552\" alt=\"dqs_squat\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8e14a129-c54f-4422-a995-128135e95c41\" />\r\n\r\n## Future work / chances for improvement:\r\nThere could be some kind of pipeline that lets you set the skinning method per-bone, but I didn't go that deep for this implementation.  I just copied the same logic as Blender's \"preserver volume\" option for armature modifiers.\r\n\r\nOther skinning methods such as DIRECT_DELTA_MUSH could be added in the future, along with some other sophisticated methods I may have never heard of.\r\n\r\n* *Bugsquad edit, closes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9235*","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5790,"closed_issues":0,"created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:48Z","closed_at":null,"due_on":null},"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-20T03:44:23Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T03:27:29Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f38a3011f2958ff811697000aee095bb5e15510f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"req